#Return Largest Number in an array

Example:
Numbers = [10,2,25,16,17,67]
Output = 67

Logic :

1) Largest Number = First Number in array(Assuming )
2) Go to each element and ask are u bigger than Largest_Number
   if yes -->Update Largest Number
   if NO --> Continue to checking further 

Numbers = [17,2,5,65,32,1,0,-1,991]
#Numbers =[]
#Numbers =[1]


size = len(Numbers)
if(size == 0):
    print("Array is empty")
elif(size == 1):
    print(Numbers[0])
else:
    Largest = Numbers[0]
    for i in range(1,size):
        if(Numbers[i]>Largest):
            Largest = Numbers[i]
    print(Largest)
